    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0728" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/12–3048</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 524</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-12-30">December 30,
                        1948</date>.<lb/>[Received January 11, 1949.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ambassador has the honor to enclose for the Department’s information an
                    Associated Press despatch datelined San Francisco, December 25, which includes a
                    list of Chinese Nationalist Government officials who have been placed on a
                    so-called “Communist blacklist”. This report is based on a radio broadcast
                    transmitted on the night of December 24 from Communist-occupied China. It is
                    understood that considerable “jamming” prevented reception in the free China
                    area.</p>
                <p>The list has been rearranged in alphabetical order for reference purposes,
                    otherwise the despatch reads as it appeared in the Shanghai English language
                    press.</p>


                <xi:include href="d591-a1.xml" xpointer="d591-a1"/>
            </div>
